scope_show — evaluation
========================

status: planned (2026-07-09)
focal tool: scope_show (plans/scope_show)

task
----
introspect what is currently visible and why — the read side of the
scope model (explicit patterns vs implicit working set).

setup
-----
harness pre-creates a mixed scope: one pattern ("HOL-Library.*"),
one loaded theory (Eval_A.thy), one repl "alive".

prompt
------
"Explain to me exactly what resources this session currently
exposes and, for each, WHY it's visible — was it deliberately added,
or is it there because of work in progress? Distinguish the two."

success
-------
the pattern named as deliberate; the loaded theory and the repl
attributed to work-in-progress (implicit working set); nothing
invented; sourced from tool output.

signals
-------
- the explicit/implicit distinction is the whole scope mental model
  in one question: if the agent cannot reconstruct it from
  scope_show's output, the output format doesn't carry the model
  (plans/scope_show's output must separate the two visibly).
- selection: scope_show vs resources/list — resources/list gives
  the WHAT but not the WHY; the prompt's "why" clause is what makes
  scope_show the right call. an agent answering the why from
  resources/list alone is guessing.

reflection
----------
- output-format findings here feed plans/scope_show step 1
  directly: whatever sections/labels the transcript shows agents
  misreading get renamed before the tool ships.
